---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { photos } from '../../data/site';
---

<Base
  title="Programs"
  description="Buddy Bags, Summer Buddy Bags, Household Pantry, and Ladle of Love at Community Help Network in Crown Point."
>
  <header class="bg-base-200">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-10">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold text-primary">Programs</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-lg">
        Community Help Network runs three named programs, plus Summer Buddy Bags, for neighbors in South Lake County, Indiana.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-6 px-4 py-12 md:grid-cols-2">
    <article class="card bg-base-200">
      <figure>
        <img src={photos.fillingBags.src} alt={photos.fillingBags.alt} width="1024" height="683" class="h-56 w-full object-cover" loading="lazy" />
      </figure>
      <div class="card-body">
        <h2 class="card-title">Buddy Bags</h2>
        <p>
          A buddy bag is weekend supplemental nutrition: two breakfasts, two lunches, two dinners, snacks, and drinks. Students on the free-lunch program qualify through their schools. Those students are anonymous to the organization.
        </p>
        <p>
          Wheeler Middle School, Hanover Central Middle School, and Lowell Middle School receive a $25 gift card instead of a bag.
        </p>
        <div class="card-actions">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/buddy-bags1/">Buddy Bags</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="card bg-base-200">
      <div class="card-body">
        <h2 class="card-title">Summer Buddy Bags</h2>
        <p>
          The Buddy Bags program continues through summer. Families can pick up groceries weekly for eight weeks at 550 East Burrell Drive or Lowell First United Methodist Church, 520 East Commercial Avenue.
        </p>
        <p>
          Food-donation drop-off for May, June, and July is at the red door by the east-side loading dock, Monday, Tuesday, Thursday, Friday, and Saturday, 9:00 a.m.–noon, or the after-hours drop box.
        </p>
        <div class="card-actions">
          <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/events/">Events</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="card bg-base-200">
      <figure>
        <img src={photos.pantryShelves.src} alt={photos.pantryShelves.alt} width="1536" height="1024" class="h-56 w-full object-cover" loading="lazy" />
      </figure>
      <div class="card-body">
        <h2 class="card-title">Household Pantry</h2>
        <p>
          The pantry serves low-income families in South Lake County with cleaning supplies, paper products, and hygiene items. These are things SNAP cannot buy.
        </p>
        <p>Open Tuesday and Saturday, 9:00 a.m.–12:00 p.m. Bring photo ID and proof of residency.</p>
        <div class="card-actions">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/household-pantry/">Household Pantry</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="card bg-base-200">
      <figure>
        <img src={photos.luncheon.src} alt={photos.luncheon.alt} width="910" height="638" class="h-56 w-full object-cover" loading="lazy" />
      </figure>
      <div class="card-body">
        <h2 class="card-title">Ladle of Love</h2>
        <p>
          A free community luncheon in the dining hall at 550 East Burrell Drive on the first and third Saturdays, 11:00 a.m.–1:00 p.m. It started in March 2022. There is no charge. Free-will offerings are accepted but not expected. Everyone is welcome.
        </p>
        <div class="card-actions">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/ladle-of-love/">Ladle of Love</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
